            "Each wattmeter measures the product of one line current and the voltage from that line to the third, so the two readings are line quantities projected on axes sixty degrees apart. Summing them recovers the total active power because the third line carries the negative sum of the other two. Subtracting them leaves a quantity proportional to the reactive power, since the projections differ in sign for the reactive component. With both relations available, the load's impedance angle follows from the ratio, which is why this single connection replaces a separate reactive-power instrument and why an operator can diagnose a poor power factor from two dial readings.",
